# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
# Unsloth's llama.cpp on CUDA, the tree both Qwen models run on and share one build dir for:
# sourced by models/qwen36-35b.env (on CUDA) and models/qwen38-flash.env, so the pin moves for both
# at once. Not a model: models/trees/ is outside the models/*.env the model list reads.
#
# The tree Unsloth Studio ships, built here from its source: upstream b11681 with Unsloth's merged
# PRs (release b11681-mix-7baeb9a, 2026-10-16). Since upstream #29751 (2026-10-01) its Qwen3.8-Flash
# sparse attention pools the indexer keys once per block and takes the top-k over blocks; the
# b11160 pin before it re-pooled the whole cache per token (T-051, T-053). The source commit is not
# fetchable from the repo, so the pin is the release tarball, with its checksum. See
# docs/qwen36.md#one-tree-for-both-qwen-models.
: "${LLAMA_REPO:=https://github.com/unslothai/llama.cpp}"
: "${LLAMA_COMMIT:=57bf43afe8a9981e33fcfc11a755bcee2b775d2d}"
: "${LLAMA_TARBALL:=$LLAMA_REPO/releases/download/b11681-mix-7baeb9a/llama.cpp-source-commit-$LLAMA_COMMIT.tar.gz}"
: "${LLAMA_TARBALL_SHA256:=57588a7e07accb66890406728ba72ce29d12f49dcc394b79813d0a8a17cfcc76}"
: "${LLAMA_DIR:=$QWEN_HOME/llama.cpp-unsloth}"
# No CCCL fetch: this tree's top-k has its own radix kernel for many rows instead of the segmented
# sort whose [depth x ubatch] temporaries ran the CUDA pool out of the card at 19-48k on b11160
# (T-049), and uses cub::DeviceTopK only from CCCL 3.4.3 (GGML_CUDA_CCCL_VERSION would fetch it).
: "${LLAMA_CMAKE_ARGS:=}"
# One patch for Qwen3.8-Flash's decode at depth: on a quantized cache a single query's attention
# still runs over every cell, the selection only masking them; patches/unsloth/ attends over the
# selected cells instead. On b11160 it took 64k from 12.9 to 16.4 tok/s and 110k from 10.5 to 14.3;
# ported to this pin, tested, not benchmarked. Qwen3.6 has no sparse attention and does not reach it.
# See docs/qwen38-flash.md#decode-at-depth.
PATCH_DIR="patches/unsloth"
